+{"schema_version":1,"plan_id":"build","node_id":"F0b","attempt":2,"source":"reviewer","source_ref":"docs/trace/build/F0b/verdicts/A1-reviewer.json: R1, R2, R3, R4, R6, R8, R9 (R5 and R7 not diagnosed: David's rulings stand)","findings":[{"id":"I1","rule_id":"none","layer":"api","files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Properties/launchSettings.json","src/Uinsure.Policies.Persistence/PersistenceServiceCollectionExtensions.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Persistence/DatabaseOptions.cs","src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Program.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: dotnet run fails at start-up with OptionsValidationException 'Database:Provider must be Sqlite or SqlServer' (orchestrator receipt). Program.cs:30 is where it shows up, not the cause. Cause: the Api project has no Development configuration file. The packet diff (diff.patch) adds no appsettings*.json path in any commit, and a Glob of src/Uinsure.Policies.Api finds only Properties/launchSettings.json, which sets only ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT (launchSettings.json:7-9). So configuration['Database:Provider'] is null at PersistenceServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:13 and DatabaseOptions.IsValid returns false for null (DatabaseOptions.cs:16-17). The first resolution of IOptions<DatabaseOptions> happens in EnsureSqliteCreated (PersistenceServiceCollectionExtensions.cs:37, called from Program.cs:30), and it throws there. This breaks the architecture Config line ('appsettings.Development.json sets Sqlite with one DB file per worktree') and requirements.md:156 ('port 5080, its own SQLite file'). Persistence green (6f9a3b6) added the provider switch with ValidateOnStart and no config to feed it. The only real-process receipt is gate.stub at ea04835 (loop.jsonl:11), which predates that commit. Fix direction: add the Development configuration that the contract names, selecting the Sqlite provider and a file-backed SQLite connection string relative to the worktree. Use no absolute path and no secret, and keep the file covered by the existing *.db ignore (.gitignore:7-9). Leave Production failing fast when unconfigured, because that is what ValidateOnStart is for. After green, re-run a real-process start plus /health/live and /health/ready on :5080. The red test is I2.","fingerprint":"none|src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/appsettings.Development.json|missing-dev-config","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given a WebApplicationFactory<Program> in the Development environment that sets neither Database:Provider nor ConnectionStrings:Policies (it may still swap TimeProvider for FakeTimeProvider) When GET /health/live and GET /health/ready Then both return 200 Healthy, and at HEAD the host fails to build with OptionsValidationException, which is the right reason for red (Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests.DevelopmentConfigurationTests, a new class with its own factory; the same test as I2)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I2","rule_id":"none","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/PoliciesApiFactory.cs","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/Support/UnreachableDatabaseApiFactory.cs"],"root_cause":"Symptom: the suite was 70/70 green while the app could not start (I1). Cause: every factory supplies the provider and the connection itself. PoliciesApiFactory.cs:34-35 sets Database:Provider=Sqlite and ConnectionStrings:Policies through UseSetting, ProductionApiFactory inherits this, and UnreachableDatabaseApiFactory.cs:23-24 sets SqlServer the same way. So no test ever resolves DatabaseOptions from the app's own appsettings files, which is the path dotnet run and Pause 2 use. The acceptance at build.dag.yaml:78 ('/health/live and /health/ready (DB) answer') was therefore proven only for injected configuration. This is a separate cause from I1 (the harness masks missing config, while I1 is the missing config), so the two are not merged. However, this finding's test is the red test for I1. Fix direction: add one integration fixture that boots Program in Development on the project's own configuration and injects nothing for