r call is removed (a mutation check recorded in the receipt). Together, the on and off tests then tell the conditional apart from no wiring.","fingerprint":"none|tests/Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests/ApplicationInsightsTests.cs|on-branch-untested","testable":true,"suggested_test":"Given the API built with APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING set to a dummy InstrumentationKey with an unroutable local IngestionEndpoint When the host is built Then RegisteredServiceTypes contains at least one OpenTelemetry or Azure.Monitor type and GET /health/live returns 200 (Uinsure.Policies.Api.Tests.ApplicationInsightsTests, with a new class fixture that sets the string)","untestable_reason":null},{"id":"I4","rule_id":"none","layer":"tests","files":[".githooks/commit-msg",".claude/hooks/guard-bash.mjs",".claude/hooks/__tests__/guards.test.mjs"],"root_cause":"Layer note: the schema has no harness value, so 'tests' is used here. The real locus is the trailer enforcement in the harness. Symptom: the builder and tester commits 91e5e2e, 19c67f6, cd0ea2b, 6f9a3b6, 3bd7a46 and fe93e5b have no Rule trailer (trailers.txt:19-23, 31-36, 83-88, 96-101, 109-114, 122-127), while 3e6726e and bec548a carry 'Rule: none' (trailers.txt:48, 67). Cause: neither enforcement point checks Rule or TDD. .githooks/commit-msg:16-25 parses and checks only Agent, Plan and Node, and the agent-side G9 guard at guard-bash.mjs:141-143 checks the same three. So an agent that leaves out Rule is never stopped, and inclusion depended on each dispatch's memory. The fixture at guards.test.mjs:238-246 has no negative case for a missing Rule or TDD. Rule violated: CLAUDE.md hard rules ('Loop commits carry the trailers Agent, Plan, Node, Rule and TDD') and requirements-trace SKILL.md:52. Fix direction: this is harness-locked, so no subagent may change it. David extends both enforcement points (and their fixtures) to require Rule and TDD on tester and builder loop commits, not on main bookkeeping commits. For the six existing F0